From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 02:19:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pyproject: ship the vendored wolfpld/etcpak licence in the
 wheel

The extension statically compiles wolfpld/etcpak (src/etcpak, a git
submodule) under its BSD-3-Clause licence, whose second clause requires
the copyright notice to be reproduced in binary redistributions. The
wheel only carries the wrapper's own MIT LICENSE: setuptools' default
licence glob looks at the project root, so src/etcpak/LICENSE.txt is
never picked up. Upstream's own PyPI wheels carry the same gap.

List both files explicitly under [tool.setuptools] license-files (the
pre-PEP 639 key, as build-system pins setuptools<72.2.0). The other two
vendored files, bc7enc.cpp and bcdec.h, are dual MIT/Unlicense with the
text kept in-source, so no separate notice is needed for them.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against K0lb3/etcpak]
---
 pyproject.toml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 798d02c..3854173 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -37,6 +37,9 @@ dynamic = ["version"]
 "Homepage" = "https://github.com/K0lb3/etcpak"
 "Bug Tracker" = "https://github.com/K0lb3/etcpak"
 
+[tool.setuptools]
+license-files = ["LICENSE", "src/etcpak/LICENSE.txt"]
+
 [tool.setuptools.dynamic]
 version = { attr = "etcpak.__version__" }
 
-- 
2.43.0

